#4000
"Elhanni River - Bend"
"Curving from northwest to southeast to accomodate the grassy bank to the

southeast, the rushing Elhanni tumbles downstream as it seaks the sea.  To the

northeast, the Cairn mountains loom, their granite crags carving a zig-zag

horizon into the sky.  The current from the north is extremely fierce, but

this bend slows the current enough for a strong swimmer.

