#4012
"Limestone Shelf - West of a Waterfall"
"A majestic waterfall crashes to the east, following a long drop from the

mountain shelf above.  The impact of the water sends a fine spray into the

air, coating this limestone shelf and creating a hazardous, slippery haven

from the rushing water of the river.  The cacaphonous sound of the falls echos

between the limestone wall to the west and the granite rock of the mountain

across the river, creating a tremendous noise which is nearly deafening.  The

shelf continues to the south along the river, and climbs to the north,

twisting up to the east.

"
