#4014
"Along a Pebbled Trail"
"A small pebbled path climbs up to the east, toward a rope bridge in the

distance.  A large, moss-covered boulder marks the western end of the

trail.  It appears to be well-traveled; the green and red mosses which

grow on it are crushed in several places, leaving boot imprints.  The

trail is bordered by a sheer rock face to the north and the gorge to the

south.

