#4017
"North End of a Rope Bridge"
"The worn ropes of this thick rope bridge do not appear overly worn or

rotting, but that does not compensate for the missing and cracked boards

which form this walkway high over the rushing river below.  To the north,

the bridge reaches a pebbled trail which graces the curve of a large

mountain.  To the south, the bridge overhangs a rocky gorge as it nears a

large, forboding forest of dark leaves.  From the west, the sound of the

river becoming a waterfall rush into your ears.

