#4025
"Atop a Boulder"
"This massive boulder sits alongside another, larger boulder to the east,

covered in moss and slime.  It is but a short hop across a narrow gap to reach

the boulder to the east, but a long descent or fall lies to the west, as the

boulder stands above a limestone shelf about thirty feet below.  A waterfall

lies to the south, pouring into a river which leads down to the west.

"
"[Phule] action climb down

[Phule] action 1 east

[Phule] action 1 west

[Phule] action jump 1 west 1 down

"
