#4026
"Atop a Moss-Covered Boulder"
"Moss covers this large boulder, its smooth, porous surface a welcome home

to the lichen and slime.  This boulder is larger and more rounded than

the dry, rough-hewn boulder a short hop to the west.  It is an easy jump

down to a pebbled trail to the east, which climbs the shoulder of the

mountain above the gorge to the south.  From below, the roaring sound of

crashing water echoes across the rocks.

"
